+## Adaptive spectral view organizer
+
+The newest layer is documented in [ADAPTIVE_VIEW_ORGANIZER_RESEARCH.md](ADAPTIVE_VIEW_ORGANIZER_RESEARCH.md).
+
+- `view_optimizer.py`: learns temporal synchronization and Fourier-bin overlap, merges consumers into lazy union caches, splits them when schedules diverge, and uses dormant probe windows to avoid overhead on stable asynchronous workloads.
+- `benchmark_view_optimizer.py`: synchronized, two-cluster, asynchronous, and regime-shift benchmarks.
+- `benchmark_view_optimizer_results.json`: captured medians and learned partitions.
+
+The regression suite now contains 34 passing tests. Generic workload clustering/materialized-view selection is prior database work; the research target here is its Fourier-specific integration with producer-side relation metadata and projected spectral state.
